# {{ .Name }}

An HTTP service laid out with [vertical slice architecture](https://github.com/cybersafetyid/featherctl/blob/main/docs/architecture.md)
and structured for use with [featherctl](https://github.com/cybersafetyid/featherctl).

## Quick start

```bash
go run ./cmd/api          # listens on :8080, override with PORT
curl localhost:8080       # add a feature first: feather new feature order
```

## Adding a feature

```bash
feather new feature order   # creates internal/features/order and wires it in
go build ./...
```

## Layout

```
cmd/api                     entry point
internal/features           one self-contained package per feature
internal/platform/router    HTTP router; feature routes are registered here
internal/platform/container dependency wiring for every feature
internal/shared/httpx       shared HTTP request/response helpers
internal/shared/validator   shared input validation helpers
```

## Development

```bash
make test     # run the test suite
make lint     # run golangci-lint
make fmt      # format the tree
make run      # start the server
```

`feather.yaml` describes where featherctl is allowed to auto-wire generated
code. `feather doctor` checks that the file, the markers it points at and the
build itself are all still healthy.
